{"spanId":"SRD521-PTG-ACTIONS-REACTIONS-001","source":{"corpus":"srd-5.2.1","path":".references/srd-5.2.1/Playing-the-Game.md","headingPath":["Actions","Reactions"],"ordinal":1,"lineStart":326,"lineEnd":326,"textHash":"8a7ede6b5f07f792"},"classification":"definition","requirementIds":["RAW-PTG-REACTIONS-001"],"text":"Reactions"}
{"spanId":"SRD521-PTG-ACTIONS-REACTIONS-002","source":{"corpus":"srd-5.2.1","path":".references/srd-5.2.1/Playing-the-Game.md","headingPath":["Actions","Reactions"],"ordinal":2,"lineStart":328,"lineEnd":328,"textHash":"46159787deb04757"},"classification":"definition","requirementIds":["RAW-PTG-REACTIONS-001"],"text":"Certain special abilities, spells, and situations allow you to take a special action called a Reaction."}
{"spanId":"SRD521-PTG-ACTIONS-REACTIONS-003","source":{"corpus":"srd-5.2.1","path":".references/srd-5.2.1/Playing-the-Game.md","headingPath":["Actions","Reactions"],"ordinal":3,"lineStart":328,"lineEnd":328,"textHash":"50d4c6e661539be1"},"classification":"rule-procedure","requirementIds":["RAW-PTG-REACTIONS-002"],"text":"A Reaction is an instant response to a trigger of some kind, which can occur on your turn or on someone else's."}
{"spanId":"SRD521-PTG-ACTIONS-REACTIONS-004","source":{"corpus":"srd-5.2.1","path":".references/srd-5.2.1/Playing-the-Game.md","headingPath":["Actions","Reactions"],"ordinal":4,"lineStart":328,"lineEnd":328,"textHash":"99799623222c8ed9"},"classification":"definition","requirementIds":["RAW-PTG-REACTIONS-003"],"text":"The Opportunity Attack, described later in \"Playing the Game,\" is the most common type of Reaction."}
{"spanId":"SRD521-PTG-ACTIONS-REACTIONS-005","source":{"corpus":"srd-5.2.1","path":".references/srd-5.2.1/Playing-the-Game.md","headingPath":["Actions","Reactions"],"ordinal":5,"lineStart":330,"lineEnd":330,"textHash":"01a9843ae00e4ed6"},"classification":"rule-consequence","requirementIds":["RAW-PTG-REACTIONS-004"],"text":"When you take a Reaction, you can't take another one until the start of your next turn."}
{"spanId":"SRD521-PTG-ACTIONS-REACTIONS-006","source":{"corpus":"srd-5.2.1","path":".references/srd-5.2.1/Playing-the-Game.md","headingPath":["Actions","Reactions"],"ordinal":6,"lineStart":330,"lineEnd":330,"textHash":"fc94e16b423f25f6"},"classification":"rule-consequence","requirementIds":["RAW-PTG-REACTIONS-005"],"text":"If the reaction interrupts another creature's turn, that creature can continue its turn right after the Reaction."}
{"spanId":"SRD521-PTG-ACTIONS-REACTIONS-007","source":{"corpus":"srd-5.2.1","path":".references/srd-5.2.1/Playing-the-Game.md","headingPath":["Actions","Reactions"],"ordinal":7,"lineStart":332,"lineEnd":332,"textHash":"1ad4e3619f18b97a"},"classification":"rule-procedure","requirementIds":["RAW-PTG-REACTIONS-006"],"text":"In terms of timing, a Reaction takes place immediately after its trigger unless the Reaction's description says otherwise."}

